  "outro": "\n    <div class=\"svc-article\">\n      <h3>How the procedure runs</h3>\n      <ol class=\"step-list\">\n        <li><b>Consultation</b>Seen by the doctor. We confirm your goals and the area, whether the procedure is suitable, and set out the expected number of sessions and the cost.</li>\n        <li><b>Harvest</b>Fat or blood is taken, according to purpose. Fat harvesting is done under local anaesthesia.</li>\n        <li><b>Processing</b>Separation and activation are carried out. You can rest during this time.</li>\n        <li><b>Application</b>The prepared cells are applied to the target area.</li>\n        <li><b>Guidance</b>We explain the after-care and the schedule for follow-up.</li>\n      </ol>\n      <p class=\"fine-note\">※ Duration varies with the type of procedure and the area. The exact schedule is given at your consultation.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"svc-article\">\n      <h3>Frequently asked questions</h3>\n      <div class=\"faq\" style=\"margin-top:18px\">\n        <details><summary>Are another person's cells introduced?</summary><div class=\"a\">No. Our adipose stem cell, PRP and PRF procedures use only the patient's own tissue and blood.</div></details>\n        <details><summary>Does it hurt a great deal?</summary><div class=\"a\">Fat harvesting is carried out under local anaesthesia. Drawing blood is at the level of an ordinary blood test. Bone marrow harvesting is comparatively uncomfortable, so we explain it fully in advance at the consultation.</div></details>\n        <details><summary>When will I feel the effect?</summary><div class=\"a\">It varies by area and by individual. Regeneration is a process that takes time, so it more usually appears gradually over weeks rather than immediately after the procedure. Wherever you hear it, an explanation that \"you will clearly see a difference within days\" is worth judging carefully.</div></details>\n        <details><summary>Is one session enough?</summary><div class=\"a\">It depends on the purpose and your condition. We set out the expected number of sessions and the intervals at the consultation before proceeding.</div></details>\n        <details><summary>Are there no side effects?</summary><div class=\"a\">Every procedure carries risk. Because your own tissue is used, the risk of rejection is relatively low, but bruising, swelling or pain at the harvest site and temporary reactions at the injection site can occur. An explanation that there are \"no side effects at all\" is hard to trust.</div></details>\n        <details><summary>Is it covered by health insurance?</summary><div class=\"a\">Mostly not. However, PRP for medial and lateral epicondylitis, and intra-articular injection of bone marrow aspirate concentrate for knee osteoarthritis, have recognised scope under the Korean system. Whether it applies in your case is confirmed at the consultation.</div></details>\n        <details><summary>Which is better, PRP or stem cells?</summary><div class=\"a\">Not \"better\" — different. PRP sends the signal for repair; stem cells introduce the working cells themselves. They are chosen according to purpose, or used together.</div></details>\n        <details><summary>Can I have this at an older age?</summary><div class=\"a\">It is true that both the number and vitality of stem cells decline with age. That is why we assess individual condition before the procedure and then judge suitability.</div></details>\n        <details><summary>Does it help with any condition at all?</summary><div class=\"a\">No. Stem cells are not a cure-all. Different conditions need different approaches. At the consultation we tell you honestly whether this procedure is appropriate, or whether another treatment would be better.</div></details>\n        <details><summary>Should I decide quickly?</summary><div class=\"a\">Not at all. Take the time to look into it thoroughly before deciding. If you wish, you are welcome to seek an opinion from another medical institution as well.</div></details>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"svc-article svc-consent\">\n      <h3>What we tell you before you decide</h3>\n      <p>Regenerative medicine is care you should agree to only after a full explanation. Before any procedure we set out the following. You have the right to ask about these points at any medical institution.</p>\n      <ul>\n        <li>whether this procedure is the standard treatment for your condition, and what other options exist</li>\n        <li>where the cells used come from, how they are separated, and by what route they are introduced</li>\n        <li>the specific effect that can be expected, and how that effect will be assessed</li>\n        <li>the risks of the procedure and the possible side effects, and what is done if they occur</li>\n        <li>the evidence behind the procedure, and whether it has national regulatory approval or review</li>\n        <li>the total cost and any costs that may arise in addition</li>\n        <li>how long, and in what way, your progress will be followed afterwards</li>\n      </ul>\n      <p>Please ask about anything you wish. Deciding once you fully understand is the best start to good care.</p>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"svc-article\">\n      <div class=\"faq\">\n        <details><summary style=\"font-size:15px\">Further reading — the academic definition of mesenchymal stem cells</summary><div class=\"a\">\n          The International Society for Cell &amp; Gene Therapy (ISCT) defines the mesenchymal stem/stromal cell (MSC) by the following three minimal criteria.\n          <ol style=\"margin-top:10px;padding-left:20px;line-height:1.8\">\n            <li>adherence to plastic under standard culture conditions</li>\n            <li>positive for CD105, CD73 and CD90, and negative for CD45, CD34, CD14 (or CD11b), CD79a (or CD19) and HLA-DR</li>\n            <li>the ability to differentiate in vitro into osteoblasts, adipocytes and chondroblasts</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div></details>\n      </div>\n    </div>",
  "cta": "\n      <h3 style=\"font-size:20px;margin-bottom:8px\">Let us decide together which approach is right for you</h3>\n      <p style=\"color:var(--gray);margin-bottom:14px\">For some people PRP is right, for others stem cells, and for some another treatment comes first.<br>We start by looking at your condition and telling you honestly.</p>\n      <p style=\"color:var(--ink);font-weight:700;margin-bottom:20px\">☎ 02-776-8768</p>\n      <a class=\"btn btn-green\" href=\"reserve\">Book a consultation</a>"
